    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field so it's returned as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` produced via MapStruct from the `Owner` entity, and the DTO is generated from the OpenAPI spec \u2014 mirroring the existing `displayName` field. So I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nResults: the new `Cp06Tests.coreComputesInitials` passes (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`), and the full suite is green (12 tests, `BUILD SUCCESS`, no regressions). `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so `charAt(0)` is always safe for a persisted owner.",
